      "result": "I rewrote `booking.py` to cover the G2 increment, and all supplied development checks now pass. I used 8 tool commands.\n\n**Changed files:** `booking.py` and `DOSSIER.md`. I did not change docs, tests, `prior/`, the `legacy_g1*.py` files or `READER_ENTRY.json`. I did not run `git status` to confirm this, because the command was blocked.\n\n**Acceptance example:**\n- `member-1` books asset A for 09:00\u201310:00 with `key-1` and gets 201.\n- The same request again gets 200 with the same ID and `replayed=True`.\n- Changing the end time under `key-1` gets 409 `idempotency-key-reused`.\n- `member-2` on A for 09:30\u201310:30 gets 409 `interval-conflict`.\n- `member-2` on A for 10:00\u201311:00 gets 201.\n- A retained AP-G1 database whose row has `starts_at=\"bad\"` raises `ValueError` and leaves the file bytes unchanged.\n\n**Commands and outcomes:**\n- **Before:** `python -m pytest -q tests` gave 17 failed and 7 passed. The old code had no validation, replay, overlap checks or migration.\n- **After:** the same command gave 17 passed and 7 subtests passed. I made no corrections after the first full run.\n- **Extra probe:** I wrote it in the scratchpad and ran it with `python -I`.\n  - The six invalid inputs returned the expected distinct 422 codes.\n  - A 24-hour interval was accepted and 24 hours plus one second was rejected.\n  - 20 rounds of 8 threads competing for one slot each gave exactly one 201 and seven 409s.\n  - A database made by `prior/booking.py` (table `g1_reservation`) is refused with `ValueError`.\n  - One line of probe output looked wrong, but my probe had reused a key after a valid request. It was not a bug in `booking.py`.\n\n**Choices of mine that the contract doesn't specify. Please confirm them:**\n- The new table is `reservations_v2` with `user_version=2`. Legacy tables stay untouched.\n- The 422 codes are `invalid-identifier`, `invalid-timestamp` and `invalid-interval`. The contract only says they must be distinct.\n- A duplicate legacy identity raises `sqlite3.IntegrityError`, because the supplied test requires it. Every other migration refusal raises `ValueError`.\n- `reserve` does not migrate. On a database that hasn't been initialized it raises `sqlite3.OperationalError`.\n\n**Remaining uncertainty:**\n- G2-OD-02 says an AI recording operator wrote it and that it is not a live owner approval. I implemented it because your task names it as part of the contract. `READER_ENTRY.json` still shows human acceptance as `PENDING`, and I have not observed any approval.\n- The `g1_reservation` table that `prior/booking.py` writes is not an authorized source, so it is refused rather than guessed. G2-OD-02 describes the retained G1 as a `reservations` table with different columns. If real data uses the `g1_reservation` shape, the owner needs to supply a mapping.\n- Concurrency evidence comes from threads in one process against local SQLite. I make no multi-process, distributed or crash-recovery claim.\n- I did not run protected acceptance or continuation. That is the operator's step.",
